From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:39:09 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 48/62] Plutonium: PipeWire video nodes for captures,
 getDisplayMedia asks the shell

EXO-CAPTURE (docs/features/CAPTURE.md):
- PlutoniumScreencast: Ash's own PipeWire producer (WebRTC's PipeWire code
  is consumer-only and off for chromeos). A frame sink video capturer on an
  output, a window (its subtree, also parked) or a tab; each frame copied
  into a MemFd (or MemPtr) buffer, BGRx or BGRA, at a fixed size,
  letterboxed. Cursor hidden, embedded (a capture overlay) or metadata
  (SPA_META_Cursor). libpipewire is loaded at run time.
- The capture command "start" (the helper's portal backend): a capture of
  kind "pipewire", its node id once PipeWire has it.
- In shell mode a page's getDisplayMedia() asks the focused shell
  ("capturerequest"), else Ash's picker, instead of Chrome's picker; the
  capture is one every shell sees, without Chrome's notification.
